\name{semantica_validate}\alias{semantica_validate}\title{Attach participant-response validation to an existing selected scale}\usage{
semantica_validate(result, responses, ordered = NULL, verbose = TRUE,
  response_analysis = NULL)
}\arguments{\item{result}{A completed high-level SEMANTICA result.}\item{responses}{Data frame or matrix containing one column for every selected item ID.}\item{ordered}{Optional ordered-item specification passed to the established response-data ESEM path.}\item{response_analysis}{Optional separate response-analysis list with estimator, ordered-item handling, model, rotation, cutoffs and criterion provenance, dataset role and overlap declaration. See \code{ACO_with_ESEM}.}\item{verbose}{Logical; print a concise completion message.}}\description{Runs the existing participant-response validation helpers on the stored selected item set and factor structure. It does not regenerate items, recompute embeddings, rerun ACO, or alter scale selection.}\details{Semantic cutoffs and score settings are never inherited. Without separately supplied response cutoffs, raw response measurements remain available and criterion attainment is unavailable. Performed, converged, admissible, and criteria-met states are reported separately.
Response fit references permit criterion comparisons without importing the semantic
optimizer's composite utility. Response composite scores remain unavailable pending
a separate response utility specification.}\value{A copy of \code{result} with response validation and updated evidence-family metadata attached.}
